<header class="page-head">
  <h1>Troubleshoot</h1>
</header>

<p class="lede">
  The first steps of <code>docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md</code>, without the
  <code>ssh</code>. The flow tester answers <em>should this work</em> from the
  configuration; it does not send a packet.
</p>

<% if Naaf::Diagnostics.enabled? %>
  <h2 class="section">Reachability</h2>
  <p class="small muted">
    The first three steps of the playbook, run from this box as the
    <code>naaf</code> user. They put real packets on the wire, so they answer a
    different question from the flow tester below: what the kernel does, not
    what the configuration says it should.
  </p>

  <div class="tools">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 class="panel-title">Ping</h3>
      <p class="small muted">Three echoes, 8-second deadline.</p>
      <form method="post" action="/troubleshoot/ping"
            hx-post="/troubleshoot/ping" hx-target="#diag-result" hx-swap="innerHTML"
            hx-disabled-elt="find button">
        <%= csrf_tag("/troubleshoot/ping") %>
        <label class="field">
          <span class="label">Host</span>
          <input class="input" type="text" name="host" placeholder="192.168.1.1" required>
        </label>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Ping</button>
        <span class="naaf-busy small muted">running…</span>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 class="panel-title">Traceroute</h3>
      <p class="small muted">One probe per hop, 12 hops.</p>
      <form method="post" action="/troubleshoot/traceroute"
            hx-post="/troubleshoot/traceroute" hx-target="#diag-result" hx-swap="innerHTML"
            hx-disabled-elt="find button">
        <%= csrf_tag("/troubleshoot/traceroute") %>
        <label class="field">
          <span class="label">Host</span>
          <input class="input" type="text" name="host" placeholder="192.0.2.1" required>
        </label>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Trace</button>
        <span class="naaf-busy small muted">running…</span>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 class="panel-title">Curl</h3>
      <p class="small muted">
        <code>tcp</code> is a bare connect — use it to ask whether a port
        answers at all.
      </p>
      <form method="post" action="/troubleshoot/curl"
            hx-post="/troubleshoot/curl" hx-target="#diag-result" hx-swap="innerHTML"
            hx-disabled-elt="find button">
        <%= csrf_tag("/troubleshoot/curl") %>
        <div class="fields">
          <label class="field grow">
            <span class="label">Host</span>
            <input class="input" type="text" name="host" placeholder="192.168.1.10" required>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span class="label">Scheme</span>
            <select class="input" name="scheme">
              <option value="tcp">tcp</option>
              <option value="http">http</option>
              <option value="https">https</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span class="label">Port</span>
            <input class="input input-port" type="number" name="port" min="1" max="65535" placeholder="443">
          </label>
        </div>
        <label class="field">
          <span class="label">Path</span>
          <input class="input" type="text" name="path" placeholder="/">
        </label>
        <p>
          <label class="choice">
            <input type="checkbox" name="insecure"> Skip TLS verification (https only)
          </label>
        </p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Request</button>
        <span class="naaf-busy small muted">running…</span>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="diag-result">
    <%= render("troubleshoot/output",
               locals: {tool: @diag_tool, result: @diag_result, error: @diag_error}) %>
  </div>

  <hr class="rule">
<% end %>

<h2 class="section">Flow tester</h2>
<p class="small muted">
  Walks a packet through the same rules the renderers emit — client
  <code>AllowedIPs</code>, cryptokey routing, the proto-158 routes, and the
  <code>inet naaf</code> forward chain — and reports which line decided it.
</p>

<form method="get" action="/troubleshoot/flow"
      hx-get="/troubleshoot/flow" hx-target="#flow-result" hx-swap="innerHTML"
      hx-disabled-elt="find button">
  <div class="fields">
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">From</span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="src" value="<%= h(request.params["src"].to_s) %>"
             placeholder="<%= h(@settings[:server_ip].to_s.sub(/\.1\z/, ".2")) %>" required>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">To</span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="dst" value="<%= h(request.params["dst"].to_s) %>"
             placeholder="192.168.1.10" required>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">Protocol</span>
      <select class="input" name="proto">
        <% Naaf::App::FLOW_PROTOS.each do |proto| %>
          <option value="<%= proto %>"<%= " selected" if request.params["proto"] == proto %>><%= proto %></option>
        <% end %>
      </select>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">Port</span>
      <input class="input" type="number" name="dport" min="1" max="65535"
             value="<%= h(request.params["dport"].to_s) %>" placeholder="443">
      <span class="help">Ignored for ICMP.</span>
    </label>
  </div>
  <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Trace</button>
  <span class="naaf-busy small muted">working…</span>
</form>

<div id="flow-result">
  <%= render("troubleshoot/flow", locals: {report: @report, error: @flow_error}) %>
</div>
